# Ship-it Process

When the user says "ship it" (or asks to release / deploy), run these steps **in order**:

## 1. Commit & tag in `rivolt`
```
git add <changed files>
git commit -m "v0.X.Y: <short summary>\n\n<detail lines>"
git tag v0.X.Y
git push --follow-tags
```
Follow the existing `v0.X.Y: <title>` commit message convention.
`--follow-tags` pushes the commit and any reachable annotated/lightweight tags in one shot.

## 2. Bump the infra chart in `rivolt-infra`
File: `apps/rivolt/app.yaml` — update the `version` field:
```yaml
chart:
  version: v0.X.Y   # bump from previous tag
```
Then:
```
cd rivolt-infra
git add apps/rivolt/app.yaml
git commit -m "rivolt: bump to v0.X.Y"
git push
```

## Version numbering
- Patch bump (`0.X.Y+1`) for fixes and small features (the usual case).
- Check `git log --oneline -1` for the last version to determine the next one.
